1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:06,165
This is a demo of the fix for ERD Studio issue seventy-six: grouping logical models by layer.

2
00:00:07,167 --> 00:00:10,462
First, the problem, on the current release.

3
00:00:11,467 --> 00:00:19,592
Every logical model lives in one flat logical-models folder. The reporter's SAP bronze tables are mixed in with the silver and gold models.

4
00:00:20,967 --> 00:00:23,597
The Model Library shows the same flat list.

5
00:00:27,467 --> 00:00:35,471
Now open the gold finance domain, and add a new dbt model, fct_revenue, from the Add Existing Model dialog.

6
00:00:40,702 --> 00:00:47,398
Its YAML file lands in the same flat folder, right next to the SAP tables. That is the issue.

7
00:00:49,202 --> 00:00:51,797
Now the same project, with the fix.

8
00:00:52,802 --> 00:01:03,292
The Model Library is still flat, and it has a new button: Organise Model Library by Layer. First, without organising anything, add fct_margin to the gold domain.

9
00:01:03,902 --> 00:01:07,099
Adding it from the dbt project, as before.

10
00:01:11,902 --> 00:01:21,778
Because this library is still flat, the new file stays at the top level. Folders are opt-in, so nothing changes for a team until someone decides to organise.

11
00:01:22,378 --> 00:01:24,118
Opting in is one command.

12
00:01:29,678 --> 00:01:39,672
It works out which layer's domains use each model, and asks first. dim_project is shared by silver and gold, so it stays at the top level, and so does the unused model.

13
00:01:40,278 --> 00:01:43,930
The library is now grouped into Bronze, Silver and Gold.

14
00:01:47,378 --> 00:01:53,123
On disk, each layer has its own folder. Domain files and layers.json did not change.

15
00:01:58,678 --> 00:02:04,011
Now that the project uses layer folders, add fct_revenue to the gold domain.

16
00:02:11,078 --> 00:02:14,533
It is created straight into logical-models/gold/.

17
00:02:18,978 --> 00:02:26,471
Later, a teammate moves dim_location out of the gold domain and into a silver one. Its file is now in the wrong layer folder.

18
00:02:28,478 --> 00:02:34,786
Running Organise again spots it: dim_location, gold to silver. Re-running is always safe.

19
00:02:42,378 --> 00:02:44,425
And the file moves into silver.

20
00:02:52,744 --> 00:02:57,409
Every canvas still resolves its models by name, whichever folder they are in.

21
00:03:03,244 --> 00:03:11,422
That's the fix. Layer folders are opt-in, one command organises the library and keeps it tidy, and domain files never change.
